@Immutable
data class SbRowStatus(val tone: SbStatusTone, val word: String? = null, val glyph: SbStatusGlyph? = null)

/**
 * A list row (spec/02 §3.3): [title] (body), [meta] (second line, caption textMuted, tabular), [text] (third line,
 * caption text); 56 / 64 / 88 dp by content. [lead] and [trail] are slots in textMuted ([trail] also caption,
 * tabular). [onClick] makes the whole row the target and adds the chevron. [hairline] = the 1 dp border line above,
 * inset 16 dp at the start: false for the first row of a group. [done] = the finished row (D83 (1)): 40 dp (48 dp
 * with [onClick], spec/02 §3.3), caption textMuted, the success glyph, no hairline, meta, text and status ignored,
 * „erledigt:“ only for screen readers. [status] (§14.4) = glyph and word at the start of the end part, and the word
 * as the row's TalkBack state, so the row is one stop. [value] (spec/02 §3.3, §14.4) = a highlighted number at the end in
 * bodyStrong, tabular. [menu] (D105 (25)) = the 48 dp „Mehr zu <title>“ button at the end with these rows and
 * [menuDanger] last; the row then has no chevron. [menuExpanded] = the menu's open state held by the app (a stateless
 * screen, a test that draws the open menu; null = the row holds it itself), [onMenuExpandedChange] its change (as
 * SbOverflowMenu's second form, §14.8; 2026-11-01, D129).
 * [enabled] = false: words and any trailing chevron in textMuted, no click or open menu, disabled semantics and
 * no hover/pressed fill. A supplied menu keeps its disabled overflow key instead of a chevron (D105 (25)).
 * [menuFocusRequester] (CHECKS.md §87; provisional, agent) addresses the ⋮ after „Rückgängig“ in every input mode, as on
 * SbPhotoThumb: with it the ⋮ can take focus under touch exploration, where the row takes none.
 */
